      "dataViz": {
        "$description": "Derived from the accent. Hues within deltaE 16 of the same mode's feedback colors are excluded (dark: about H 140-160 and 0-40 near success and warning/error at their lightness; light: H 0-60 and 130-170). series.1 keeps the accent hue: the dark accent (brand yellow, OKLCH L 0.81) sits above the dark band 0.48-0.67, so dark series.1 is H 80 L 0.65 C 0.13; the light accent (amber L 0.46) is too close to light warning, so light series.1 is H 68 L 0.61 C 0.13. Slots 2-6 were picked by farthest-point search under the tokens-schema 6.3 checks, then ordered for the largest worst adjacent CVD distance. Per slot (H; light L C; dark L C): 1 (68/80; 0.61 0.13; 0.65 0.13), 2 (305/310; 0.58 0.18; 0.60 0.15), 3 (330/150; 0.44 0.15; 0.56 0.15), 4 (225/255; 0.60 0.11; 0.64 0.18), 5 (265/181; 0.44 0.11; 0.62 0.11), 6 (270/280; 0.62 0.18; 0.56 0.18). Result light / dark: worst adjacent CVD deltaE 15.3 / 17.7, worst adjacent normal-vision deltaE 16.0 / 18.5, nearest feedback color 16.3 / 16.2, lowest contrast against the four surfaces 3.12 / 3.21. sequential: accent hue, low to high magnitude, light L 0.93 to 0.45, dark L 0.33 to 0.81 (step 5 is the brand yellow). diverging: blue H 255 (negative) to the accent hue (positive) through a neutral midpoint (neutral.200 light, neutral.700 dark); light L 0.46 / 0.74 / mid / 0.80 / 0.55, dark L 0.74 / 0.48 / mid / 0.52 / 0.80.",
        "$extensions": {
          "com.design-extract": {
            "confidence": "derived"
